{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/872805-beasts-integrity","id":872805,"title":"Beasts & Integrity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-23T19:11:03-07:00","id":872805,"title":"Beasts & Integrity","content":"So while I've been reading the book , I am confused how Beasts suffer with mental trauma. Is there a stat that expresses this mechanically like humanity or morality or the like? Assistance on understanding this would be appreciated!<br /> <br /> And if this case is Beasts do not have integrity - how do they manage mental health? Can a Beast not feel psychological torture and how would it work in terms of game mechanics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","user":"Volke","date":". 04-23-2016, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:10:44-07:00","id":872828,"title":"","content":"Beasts don't have an Integrity score; it's replaced by Satiety. Their mental health, you could say, is reliant on how well they're fed.<br /> <br /> Psychological trauma might still be a problem for the Begotten, but it's not represented by a dot rating like with mortals. That's more of a roleplaying consideration. Most of their problems are social fallout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:37:36-07:00","id":872841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/872805-beasts-integrity?p=872828#post872828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts don't have an Integrity score; it's replaced by Satiety. Their mental health, you could say, is reliant on how well they're fed.<br /> <br /> Psychological trauma might still be a problem for the Begotten, but it's not represented by a dot rating like with mortals. That's more of a roleplaying consideration. Most of their problems are social fallout.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see... Well for example: I was thinking of ideas like if a Begotten was captured and tortured by like an enemy faction or the like. Could I apply a derangement or what would be the best idea to use this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:40:04-07:00","id":872842,"title":"","content":"Oh, in that case, Conditions would probably serve you well. Tilts too, depending on how the scene is playing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:51:39-07:00","id":872857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/872805-beasts-integrity?p=872842#post872842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, in that case, Conditions would probably serve you well. Tilts too, depending on how the scene is playing out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well my issue with conditions is things like Broken for example:<br /> <br /> For a few conditions in the Beast book like Broken: to resolve the condition you need to regain a dot of integrity, lose another dot of integrity or achieve an exceptional success on a breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T21:00:31-07:00","id":872863,"title":"","content":"It's easy enough to make up your own Conditions, or change the parameters of an existing one. So, since Beasts don't have Integrity, the resolution for Broken might be &quot;You get an exceptional success or dramatic failure on a roll that uses Resolve&quot; or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}